    "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The equation <math alttext=\"x plus y equals 1,440\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1,440</mn></math> represents the number of minutes of daylight (between sunrise and sunset), <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math>, and the number of minutes of non-daylight, <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math>, on a particular day in Oak Park, Illinois. If this day has <math alttext=\"670\"><mn>670</mn></math> minutes of daylight, how many minutes of non-daylight does it have?</p>",
    "type": "mcq",
    "correctAnswer": "B",
    "explanation": "<p>Choice B is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the equation <math alttext=\"x plus y equals 1,440\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1,440</mn></math> represents the number of minutes of daylight, <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math>, and the number of minutes of non-daylight, <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math>, on a particular day in Oak Park, Illinois. It&rsquo;s also given that this day has <math alttext=\"670\"><mn>670</mn></math> minutes of daylight. Substituting <math alttext=\"670\"><mn>670</mn></math> for <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> in the equation <math alttext=\"x plus y equals 1,440\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1,440</mn></math> yields <math alttext=\"670 plus y equals 1,440\"><mn>670</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1,440</mn></math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"670\"><mn>670</mn></math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"y equals 770\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>770</mn></math>. Therefore, this day has <math alttext=\"770\"><mn>770</mn></math> minutes of non-daylight.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the number of minutes of daylight, not non-daylight, on this day.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is the total number of minutes of daylight and non-daylight.</p>",
