    "subtopicId": "linear-equations-two-variables",
    "subtopic": "Linear equations in two variables",
    "difficulty": "easy",
    "stem": "<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">A city&rsquo;s total expense budget for one year was <span class=\"italic\">x</span> million dollars. The city budgeted <span class=\"italic\">y</span> million dollars for departmental expenses and 201 million dollars for all other expenses. Which of the following represents the relationship between <span class=\"italic\">x</span> and <span class=\"italic\">y</span> in this context?</p>",
    "type": "mcq",
    "correctAnswer": "B",
    "explanation": "<p>Choice B is correct. Of the city&rsquo;s total expense budget for one year, the city budgeted <span class=\"italic\">y</span> million dollars for departmental expenses and 201 million dollars for all other expenses. This means that the expression <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y plus 201\"></span> represents the total expense budget, in millions of dollars, for one year. It&rsquo;s given that the total expense budget for one year is <span class=\"italic\">x</span> million dollars. It follows then that the expression <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y plus 201\"></span> is equivalent to <span class=\"italic\">x</span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y plus 201, equals x\"></span>. Subtracting <span class=\"italic\">y</span> from both sides of this equation yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"201 equals, x minus y\"></span>. By the symmetric property of equality, this is the same as <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x minus y, equals 201\"></span>.<p>Choices A and C are incorrect. Because it&rsquo;s given that the total expense budget for one year, <span class=\"italic\">x</span> million dollars, is comprised of the departmental expenses, <span class=\"italic\">y</span> million dollars, and all other expenses, 201 million dollars, the expressions <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x plus y\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 x minus y  \"></span> both must be equivalent to a value greater than 201 million dollars. Therefore, the equations <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x plus y, equals 201 \"></span>and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 x minus y, equals 201 \"></span>aren&rsquo;t true. Choice D is incorrect. The value of <span class=\"italic\">x </span>must be greater than the value of <span class=\"italic\">y</span>. Therefore, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y minus x, equals 201\"></span> can&rsquo;t represent this relationship.</p><p> </p></p>",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "A",
        "text": "<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x plus y, equals 201\"></span></span></p>"
      },
      {
        "id": "B",
        "text": "<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x minus y, equals 201\"></span></span></p>"
      },
      {
        "id": "C",
        "text": "<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 x minus y, equals 201\"></span></span></p>"
      },
      {
        "id": "D",
        "text": "<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y minus x, equals 201\"></span></span></p>"
      }
    ]
