    "stem": "<p>A total of <math alttext=\"364\"><mn>364</mn></math> paper straws of equal length were used to construct two types of polygons: triangles and rectangles. The triangles and rectangles were constructed so that no two polygons had a common side. The equation <math alttext=\"3 x plus 4 y equals 364\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>364</mn>\n</mrow></math> represents this situation, where <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> is the number of triangles constructed and <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math> is the number of rectangles constructed. What is the best interpretation of <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis equals left parenthesis 24 comma 73 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>24</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>73</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> in this context?</p>",
