    "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A store sells two different-sized containers of blueberries. The store&rsquo;s sales of these blueberries totaled <math alttext=\"896.86\"><mn>896.86</mn></math> dollars last month. The equation <math alttext=\"4.51 x plus 6.07 y equals 896.86\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>4.51</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>6.07</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>896.86</mn>\n</mrow></math> represents this situation, where <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> is the number of smaller containers sold and <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math> is the number of larger containers sold. According to the equation, what is the price, in dollars, of each smaller container?</p>",
